---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Competitive Intelligence for B2B SaaS"
  description="Evidence-backed competitive intelligence for B2B SaaS teams: competitor discovery, source verification, decision analysis and executive-ready outputs."
  path="/competitive-intelligence/"
>
  <main class="svc">
    <section class="svc__hero" data-surface="dark">
      <div class="container-wide svc__hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="label">COMPETITIVE INTELLIGENCE</span>
          <h1>Know what changed, who matters, and what the evidence supports.</h1>
          <p>Evidence Axis researches public competitive signals for B2B SaaS decisions. The work starts with discovery, opens the underlying sources, separates fact from inference, and ends with a decision-ready view.</p>
          <div class="svc__actions">
            <a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=complimentary-brief">Request My Complimentary Brief <span>→</span></a>
            <a href="/sample-report/">See a public sample →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside>
          <small class="mono">EVIDENCE AXIS METHOD</small>
          <strong>Discover → Verify → Decide → Respond</strong>
          <p>Search is used to find leads. Material claims are verified by opening the source before they enter the analysis.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section svc__section">
      <div class="container-wide svc__split">
        <div>
          <span class="label">WHAT THE WORK COVERS</span>
          <h2>Competitive intelligence tied to a decision.</h2>
          <p>The scope can include competitor discovery, product and pricing changes, positioning, launches, integrations, funding or expansion signals, and the evidence behind public claims. The point is not to collect every mention. It is to determine which signals can change the decision in front of the team.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="svc__cards">
          <article><b>01</b><h3>Competitive set discovery</h3><p>Find candidates outside the names already on the team’s radar, then verify whether they belong in the set.</p></article>
          <article><b>02</b><h3>Source verification</h3><p>Open the underlying pages and preserve review dates, contradictions and evidence boundaries.</p></article>
          <article><b>03</b><h3>Decision analysis</h3><p>Connect product, pricing, positioning and recent moves to the specific business question.</p></article>
          <article><b>04</b><h3>Executive output</h3><p>Deliver the conclusion in an executive deck with a separate evidence appendix and source register.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section svc__section svc__section--paper">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <span class="label">EVIDENCE STANDARD</span>
        <h2>Fact, Inference and Unknown stay separate.</h2>
        <div class="svc__states">
          <article><strong>FACT</strong><p>Directly supported by a checked source.</p></article>
          <article><strong>INFERENCE</strong><p>An analytical conclusion built from disclosed evidence.</p></article>
          <article><strong>UNKNOWN</strong><p>Public evidence is not strong enough to claim certainty.</p></article>
        </div>
        <p class="svc__note">Vendor comparison pages and search snippets can help discovery, but they are not treated as neutral verification for material claims.</p>
        <a href="/method/">Read the full method →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section svc__faq">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <span class="label">COMMON QUESTIONS</span>
        <h2>What this service is — and is not.</h2>
        <details><summary>Is Evidence Axis a monitoring software platform?</summary><p>No. Evidence Axis is a competitive intelligence and decision-support service. Ongoing monitoring is available through Competitive Radar, but the work is human-reviewed rather than an automated feed presented as analysis.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need to provide a competitor list?</summary><p>No. A list is useful context, but discovery is part of the method. For a Complimentary Brief, known competitors are optional.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What sources are used?</summary><p>Lawful public sources. Source classes are disclosed, and material factual claims are checked against the underlying source before use.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What do I receive?</summary><p>Scope varies by engagement. The Complimentary Brief normally includes an Executive Intelligence Deck and an Evidence Appendix with sources, classifications and review dates.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section svc__cta" data-surface="dark">
      <div class="container svc__cta-inner">
        <span class="label">SEE THE WORK FIRST</span>
        <h2>Request company-specific competitive intelligence.</h2>
        <p>Use a verified work email. Evidence Axis will review the company details and confirm the research queue and delivery window by email.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=complimentary-brief">Request My Complimentary Brief <span>→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
.svc{background:#fff}.svc__hero{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff;padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5.6rem) 0}.svc__hero-grid,.svc__split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.08fr .92fr;gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem);align-items:start}.svc__hero h1,.svc h2{margin:.55rem 0 .9rem;font-size:clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5rem);line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.05em}.svc__hero p,.svc__section p,.svc__faq p,.svc__cta p{line-height:1.65}.svc__hero p{max-width:54rem;color:#b9c7d8}.svc__hero aside{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid rgba(120,160,210,.2);border-radius:.8rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03)}.svc__hero aside small{display:block;color:#8eb6e6;margin-bottom:.55rem}.svc__hero aside strong{font-size:1.3rem}.svc__hero aside p{font-size:.88rem;margin:.7rem 0 0}.svc__actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.9rem;align-items:center;margin-top:1.3rem}.svc__actions>a:not(.btn),.svc__section a{color:#8b5b34;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}.svc__section{background:#fff}.svc__section--paper{background:#f3eee6}.svc__section>div>p,.svc__cards p,.svc__faq p{color:var(--text-muted)}.svc__cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.75rem}.svc__cards article,.svc__states article{padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.12);border-radius:.75rem;background:#fff}.svc__cards b{font:800 .58rem/1 var(--font-mono);color:#496d99}.svc__cards h3{margin:.5rem 0 .3rem}.svc__cards p{margin:0;font-size:.86rem}.svc__states{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.75rem;margin:1.2rem 0}.svc__states strong{font:800 .72rem/1 var(--font-mono);letter-spacing:.07em}.svc__states p{margin:.5rem 0 0}.svc__note{max-width:62rem}.svc__faq details{border-top:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.15);padding:1rem 0}.svc__faq details:last-of-type{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.15)}.svc__faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem}.svc__faq details p{max-width:66rem;margin:.7rem 0 0}.svc__cta{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.svc__cta-inner{text-align:center;max-width:66rem}.svc__cta-inner p{color:#a8b8cb;max-width:50rem;margin:.8rem auto 1.2rem}@media(max-width:860px){.svc__hero-grid,.svc__split{grid-template-columns:1fr}.svc__states{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:560px){.svc__cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.svc__actions{display:grid}.svc__actions a{width:100%}}
</style>
